:"2016-12-08T17:53:32-08:00","id":1014545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1014533#post1014533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Requiem art is generally very good, however, I get from Fat Larry that this book had photoshoped pictures of LARP and models which is exactly the thing I don't want to see in Requiem books.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a number of pictures that appear to be edited photographs, but they don't look like your bog standard LARPer in a generic pose sort of photos, and the photoshop isn't too egregious in most of them. Besides, the book is supposed to be a collection of in-universe documents, so it <i>makes sense</i> for the pictures to be photographs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:04:50-08:00","id":1014552,"title":"","content":"Re: Mass cloning.<br /> <br /> Arguably you could do it to protect the masquerade. Literally no one would see that happening and go &quot;oh hey, Vampires.&quot; And it would, in fact, distract everyone from say another huge masquerade blunder because lbh, people would talk about it. A lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T21:58:43-08:00","id":1014614,"title":"","content":"Is anyone else confused by the way the Oath of Matrimony works with regard to social merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T23:04:14-08:00","id":1014626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1014614#post1014614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone else confused by the way the Oath of Matrimony works with regard to social merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, let's say one partner has Barfly, Invictus Status 2, Library 1, Retainer 3, Safe Place 3, and Staff 4. The other partner has Inspiring, Lancea et Sanctum status 3, Library 3, Retainer 1, Safe Place 3, and Staff 1. The former gains Inspiring, Lancea et Sanctum Status 1, one more dot of Library, and one more dot of either Safe Place or Staff. The latter gains Barfly, Invictus Status 1, one more dot of Retainer, and one more dot of either Safe Place or Staff (which ever the former didn't take).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T23:19:43-08:00","id":1014631,"title":"","content":"So Question did the two dot Not a member Covenant merits make it into the book? Like Casual User for the Carthians?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T00:07:41-08:00","id":1014639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1014631#post1014631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arr