longer do so, thanks for the warning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T13:28:51-08:00","id":1014924,"title":"","content":"Most of the art inside doesn't seem to be of the CGI-with-paint style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T15:48:28-08:00","id":1014978,"title":"","content":"So... anyone else notice the Chorister merit is much much better than each of the other pre-status merits? Like it's almost to the point of ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:15:13-08:00","id":1014990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1014978#post1014978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... anyone else notice the Chorister merit is much much better than each of the other pre-status merits? Like it's almost to the point of ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, it's the Carthian and Invictus versions that are weaker than the orher three. Chorister, Laity, and Independent Study all allow the character to learn the Covenant's brand of Sorcery if they have a teacher. It's just that the Circle of the Crone is more liberal with teaching their Sorcery Discipline to preliminary members than the Lancea et Sanctum or the Ordo Dracul (and the Ordo is more strict about it than the Lance, if the presentation is any indication). Although, the Circle only allows Choristers to learn the first dot of Cruac. Technically Sanctified Laity can learn up to five dots of Theban if their teacher is willing to place that much trust in them, and Independent Scholars can learn any number of Coils and Scales that their mentors are willing to risk teaching them under the table. On the other hand, Choristers can learn Acolyte Merits, so that's a pretty significant perk. One Foot in the Door doesn't allow you to be a leige in Invictus Oaths, but it doesn't explicitly disallow it like Casual User does for Carthian Law. Although, Casual Users do get a vote, just like Status-carrying Carthians do.<br /> <br /> This actually just further emphasizes why I like that they're separate merits. They tell us a lot about the cultures of the Covenants and how much each Covenant trusts it's preliminary members with its secrets, relative to the other four.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-09-2016, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:35:59-08:00","id":1014998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1014990#post1014990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strictly speaking, it's the Carthian and Invictus versions that are weaker than the orher three. Chorister, Laity, and Independent Study all allow the character to learn the Covenant's brand of Sorcery if they have a teacher. It's just that the Circle of the Crone is more liberal with teaching their Sorcery Discipline to preliminary members than the Lancea et Sanctum or the Ordo Dracul (and the Ordo is more strict about it than the Lance, if the presentation is any indication). Although, the Circle only allows Choristers to learn the first dot of Cruac. Technically Sanctified Laity can learn up to five dots of Theban if their teacher is willing to place that much trust in them, and Casual Users can learn any number of Coils and Scales that their mentors are willing to risk teaching them under the table. On the other hand, Choristers can learn Acolyte Merits, so that's a pretty significant perk. One Foot in the Door doesn't allow you to be a leige in Invictus Oaths, but it doesn't explicitly disallow it like Casual User does for Carthian Law. Although, Casual Users do get a vote, just like Status-carrying Carthians do.<br /> <br /> This actually just further emphasizes why I like that they're separate merits. They tell us a lot about the cultures of the Covenants and how much each Covenant trusts it's preliminary members with its secrets, relative to the other four.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The lack of thematic parallelism justified each of those merits having separate descriptions. Really cool stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:36:20-08:00","id":1015000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1014916#post1014916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. No I HATE EVERYTHING. <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you whine about everything?<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't like the art. I'm not the only one. There are plenty(PLENTY) of other things I LOVE about OP. The art in this book is not one of them. Sorry you disagree.<br /> <br /> <br /> Disagreeing with me is cool. Just, maybe try not to be an asshole about it? Or maybe not single me out and go after the others you disagree with? <br /> <br /> Plenty of options available.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to be an asshole, Larry, just poking fun at the fact that I saw you say you aren't happy with the authors in one thread and you aren't happy with the art here, I had to wonder what was bringing you back to these books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:36:22-08:00","id":1015001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1014990#post1014990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strictly speaking, it's the Carthian and Invictus versions that are weaker than the orher three. Chorister, Laity, and Independent Study all allow the character to learn the Covenant's brand of Sorcery if they have a teacher. It's just that the Circle of the Crone is more liberal with teaching their Sorcery Discipline to preliminary members than the Lancea et Sanctum or the Ordo Dracul (and the Ordo is more strict about it than the Lance, if the presentation is any indication). Although, the Circle only allows Choristers to learn the first dot of Cruac. Technically Sanctified Laity can learn up to five dots of Theban if their teacher is willing to place that much trust in them, and Casual Users can learn any number of Coils and Scales that their mentors are willing to risk teaching them under the table. On the other hand, Choristers can learn Acolyte Merits, so that's a pretty significant perk. One Foot in the Door doesn't allow you to be a leige in Invictus Oaths, but it doesn't explicitly disallow it like Casual User does for Carthian Law. Although, Casual Users do get a vote, just like Status-carrying Carthians do.<br /> <br /> This actually just further emphasizes why I like that they're separate merits. They tell us a lot about the cultures of the Covenants and how much each Covenant trusts it's preliminary members with its secrets, relative to the other four.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh given the taboo nature of it in the other two, I don't see it as likely you'd get that far, let alone anything further than a dot. But yeah, the openness of it combined with it being the ONLY one that provides access to the covenant merits sort of skews it, even compared to the other 'mystic' covenants.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I do agree they're better as separate merits, mind, I just think they should either be different ratings or mechanically close to each other in potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:46:01-08:00","id":1015008,"title":"","content":"Go it! XD<br /> <br /> Went straight to my favorite Covenant's section and already finished that, was everything I had hoped for and more. I do love how the narrative is layed out too, even in one Covenant's section you still learn so many cool things about the others and about both the setting and what can be done with the setting. Excellent work OP. ^_^<br /> <br /> (P.S. Just my own two cents, thought the art was pretty cool. Very thematic to the stories and found it immersive. Wasn't Mummy the Curse levels of good, but few things are eh?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:38:19-08:00","id":1015029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1014978#post1014978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... anyone else notice the Chorister merit is much much better than each of the other pre-status merits? Like it's almost to the point of ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also the only one that potentially lowers your Humanity cap. And simply learning Cruac is a Humanity 4 Breaking Point, so it does come with some potential Drawbacks.<br /> <br /> I don't see how it's ridiculous, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:52:46-08:00","id":1015035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015000#post1015000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not trying to be an asshole, Larry, just poking fun at the fact that I saw you say you aren't happy with the authors in one thread and you aren't happy with the art here, I had to wonder what was bringing you back to these books.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. Long day at work. <br /> <br /> The great art, amazing stories, and top notch quality does. I'm not a fan of one writer that works for OP. Just one. And 95% of the books that OP pumps out, have been great. WoD and CroD. Deviant, is probably my most anticipated. Next to HtR20, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:54:20-08:00","id":1015039,"title":"","content":"Also consider that Independent Study doesn't strictly disallow developing/creating your own coil. Consider a Crone with Independent Study, who develops a Cruac centric coil. Or a modified Coil of the Wyrm that lets them to not leash their beasts but become one with them (Without falling into Dragur status).<br /> <br /> Of course some Dragon's might take offense to it. Political drama can be fun~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11516,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11516-forgelineage","user":"ForgeLineage","date":". 12-09-2016, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11516-forgelineage","name":"ForgeLineage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T18:01:44-08:00","id":1015044,"title":"","content":"Using an Easter egg no one ever noticed in <b>Testament of Longinus</b>, <i>seven years after the fact</i>, really floored me (or was it just me who never noticed?) That was awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-09-2016, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T18:13:05-08:00","id":1015055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForgeLineage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015039#post1015039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also consider that Independent Study doesn't strictly disallow developing/creating your own coil. Consider a Crone with Independent Study, who develops a Cruac centric coil. Or a modified Coil of the Wyrm that lets them to not leash their beasts but become one with them (Without falling into Dragur status).<br /> <br /> Of course some Dragon's might take offense to it. Political drama can be fun~</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fantastic idea, holy crap!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T18:19:03-08:00","id":1015058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015029#post1015029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also the only one that potentially lowers your Humanity cap. And simply learning Cruac is a Humanity 4 Breaking Point, so it does come with some potential Drawbacks.<br /> <br /> I don't see how it's ridiculous, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yeah, but I don't see how adding the option is in any way a drawback. That's a drawback to the power itself. The merit doesn't cause that drawback since you don't HAVE to take it. Plus, what Humanity 10-seeking Vampire is joining the Circle's Chorus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T18:23:28-08:00","id":1015061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1014862#post1014862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I like the Not-A-Member Merita being listed separately, even if it did eat some wordcount. I cant imagine a phrasing of a single Merit that you could apply to any Covenant that wouldn't be clunky and awkward, especially with the different Social Merits. Plus I appreciate them having names that are thematically appropriate to the Covenant, instead of a generic catch-all name like &amp;quot;Covenant Pledge&amp;quot; or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was sort of my goal. I wanted to use the space to make some statements about the groups at large, and how they could generally organize and relate to outsiders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T18:35:04-08:00","id":1015069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015061#post1015061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was sort of my goal. I wanted to use the space to make some statements about the groups at large, and how they could generally organize and relate to outsiders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mission accomplished, if you ask me! It's subtle, but they really do say a lot about the Covenants and their attitudes towards their non-member allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T19:40:17-08:00","id":1015104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015058#post1015058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, yeah, but I don't see how adding the option is in any way a drawback. That's a drawback to the power itself. The merit doesn't cause that drawback since you don't HAVE to take it. Plus, what Humanity 10-seeking Vampire is joining the Circle's Chorus?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Merit doesn't give the Drawback, but learning Cruac does. All the Merit does that ther others don't is open up the possibility of being able to pay for other Merits and Cruac.<br /> <br /> What is your issue, if not a problem with other people learning a single dot of Cruac, while still having to pay for it? And if that is your problem, how is making it available to everyone unfair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T19:45:04-08:00","id":1015105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015104#post1015104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Merit doesn't give the Drawback, but learning Cruac does. All the Merit does that ther others don't is open up the possibility of being able to pay for other Merits and Cruac.<br /> <br /> What is your issue, if not a problem with other people learning a single dot of Cruac, while still having to pay for it? And if that is your problem, how is making it available to everyone unfair?</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue is it opening up comparatively more options than the other similarly priced merits, is all. Yes, all it does is give options, but if that's a major facet of similar merits, they should provide a similar array of options or else have a different cost, in my opinion. If opening up options is effectively worth nothing, after all, why need a merit for it to begin with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T19:52:50-08:00","id":1015113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015105#post1015105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue is it opening up comparatively more options than the other similarly priced merits, is all. Yes, all it does is give options, but if that's a major facet of similar merits, they should provide a similar array of options or else have a different cost, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's meant to show that any vampire can do Cruac. It's in their blood already. The Circle is just gathering it, they are not controllers of it like the Lance is Theban scrolls, which they hold the secret to, or Carthian Democracy magic, which is limited to the Carthians.<br /> <br /> As for costs, the Merit is incredibly cheap already for what it does. Even though the Invictus doesn't get any extra Merits they can buy, they are still getting a variable Social Merit, a Social interaction bonus, and potentially two dots of Status. Why should the Crone one throw on an Experience tax when the Merit itself doesn't give you anything, and any Merits bought through it would already be costing Experiences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T20:05:04-08:00","id":1015124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015044#post1015044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using an Easter egg no one ever noticed in <b>Testament of Longinus</b>, <i>seven years after the fact</i>, really floored me (or was it just me who never noticed?) That was awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my gosh, are you referring to the missing stanzas? Because that story in the Sanctified section is my absolute favorite! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly that level of detail was what exceeded my expectations for Secrets of the Covenants. I never expected the Onyx Path to purposefully plant story seeds in the literal text of the books themselves, and respect the hell out of the writers for doing that. Absolutely brilliant!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T20:13:16-08:00","id":1015132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015113#post1015113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it's meant to show that any vampire can do Cruac. It's in their blood already. The Circle is just gathering it, they are not controllers of it like the Lance is Theban scrolls, which they hold the secret to, or Carthian Democracy magic, which is limited to the Carthians.<br /> <br /> As for costs, the Merit is incredibly cheap already for what it does. Even though the Invictus doesn't get any extra Merits they can buy, they are still getting a variable Social Merit, a Social interaction bonus, and potentially two dots of Status. Why should the Crone one throw on an Experience tax when the Merit itself doesn't give you anything, and any Merits bought through it would already be costing Experiences?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the circle one also gives similar things, and then piles that on top. I feel that the added benefits of opening up options that characters otherwise couldn't access is worth a bit more.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I do feel we're sort of repeating ourselves now, though, and I've made my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 12-10-2016, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T20:45:32-08:00","id":1015146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015124#post1015124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh my gosh, are you referring to the missing stanzas? Because that story in the Sanctified section is my absolute favorite! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's the one. I've read <b>ToL </b>cover to cover a couple of times, and I <i>never </i>noticed that. It's such a cool setup, especially considering what creatures Eschaton 7 seems to be referring to...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T08:38:09-08:00","id":1015257,"title":"","content":"Maybe if some of the font choices didn't give me a headache I probably would have enjoyed the read a bit more. <br /> <br /> The clan books were mostly story but even they gave more options of potential storyteller tools. <br /> <br /> I was a little disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T08:52:32-08:00","id":1015258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015257#post1015257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe if some of the font choices didn't give me a headache I probably would have enjoyed the read a bit more. <br /> <br /> The clan books were mostly story but even they gave more options of potential storyteller tools. <br /> <br /> I was a little disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the exact opposite. What I'be read of the clanbooks was neat, but it never did much for me. Secrets has given me tons of international settings that I can sink my teeth into (bad pun, I know). In fact, it's inspired me to go back and give the clan books a real chance, and I am finding them much more enjoyable. <br /> <br /> My expectations have been far exceeded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T13:10:30-08:00","id":1015346,"title":"","content":"Berlin's really gone to shit, wow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T19:45:58-08:00","id":1015489,"title":"","content":"While I enjoyed the Invictus section, I have to wonder why it was set in San Diego of all places. When V20 decided to visit my hometown in the Companion, I chuckled at it describing the tourist-friendly Gaslamp as a dangerous place where people go missing, but at least that's a real part of town; the bits in <i>Secrets</i> could've been set anywhere. I had to laugh at the idea of an armed militia springing up in a touristy college town with incredibly strict gun laws, and was sad to see none of the local flavor make it into the fiction whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Is this how people living elsewhere always feel when their cities are visited in roleplaying?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 12-10-2016, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T19:52:27-08:00","id":1015492,"title":"","content":"Human only Supernatural Merit for purposes of Coil of Zirnitra, Clear Sighted? Corebook pg 299. It doesn't say Supernatural Merit in that section but it seems to fit the definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T20:02:52-08:00","id":1015498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015489#post1015489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I enjoyed the Invictus section, I have to wonder why it was set in San Diego of all places. When V20 decided to visit my hometown in the Companion, I chuckled at it describing the tourist-friendly Gaslamp as a dangerous place where people go missing, but at least that's a real part of town; the bits in <i>Secrets</i> could've been set anywhere. I had to laugh at the idea of an armed militia springing up in a touristy college town with incredibly strict gun laws, and was sad to see none of the local flavor make it into the fiction whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Is this how people living elsewhere always feel when their cities are visited in roleplaying?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that Calgary or Halifax have ever been visited, but every time Dubai has cropped up in CofD, it has been spot on. Including in this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T20:12:54-08:00","id":1015505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015498#post1015498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know that Calgary or Halifax have ever been visited, but every time Dubai has cropped up in CofD, it has been spot on. Including in this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must be a fluke, then. It was just weird to see a story about San Diego that didn't touch on the Navy presence, the local university, the Mexican or Japanese communities, or the beach and the tourists it brings. If the story hadn't said it was here, I honestly would've assumed somewhere in Arizona, the kind of place where folks actually have guns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T21:00:02-08:00","id":1015520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015489#post1015489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I enjoyed the Invictus section, I have to wonder why it was set in San Diego of all places. When V20 decided to visit my hometown in the Companion, I chuckled at it describing the tourist-friendly Gaslamp as a dangerous place where people go missing, but at least that's a real part of town; the bits in <i>Secrets</i> could've been set anywhere. I had to laugh at the idea of an armed militia springing up in a touristy college town with incredibly strict gun laws, and was sad to see none of the local flavor make it into the fiction whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Is this how people living elsewhere always feel when their cities are visited in roleplaying?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a mixed bag for me. Masquerade did Denver in an introductory adventure (Alien Hunger), and it was <i>awful</i>. Not only could it have been set anywhere, they also included completely made-up locations when there are real places that could have served the same roles (the Prince owned a club called &quot;The 13th Diocese&quot; or something, which doesn't exist, but there is an actual goth club called The Church that is actually a converted church). Also there was a sidebar witj mechanics for a practice the young vampires apparently call cow tipping - sneaking out to fields to feed on cows. In a story set in Denver. One of the 20 most populated cities in the country.<br /> <br /> Hunting Ground: the Rockies was much better overall, although it still missed on a few points, like getting the location of the Pearl Street mall wrong, and having Max Roman own a skyscraper that doesn't actually exist but is still mentioned to be one of the biggest in the city. When there's a perfectly good 1st Bank building, which is actually one of tallest in the city, and is probably the most distinctive part of Denver's skyline and sort of looks like a bird's beak. But I forgive those missteps because it gets more right than it gets wrong.<br /> <br /> I'm also pretty used to fictional stories set in Colorado just completely making up specific locations. Like The Last of Us - there is no University of Eastern Colorado (nor do any of the game's locations actually exist). Community - there is no Greendale Comminity College (and no Greendale). Often Colorado just ends up being a name to put to generic mountainous settings.<br /> <br /> Anyway, sorry for the tangent. Point is, yeah, when fiction you like is set in a place you know well, it's exciting to see the points they get right and disappointing to see the parts they get wrong. Thorough research goes a long way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T21:45:18-08:00","id":1015538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015520#post1015520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been a mixed bag for me. Masquerade did Denver in an introductory adventure (Alien Hunger), and it was <i>awful</i>. Not only could it have been set anywhere, they also included completely made-up locations when there are real places that could have served the same roles (the Prince owned a club called &quot;The 13th Diocese&quot; or something, which doesn't exist, but there is an actual goth club called The Church that is actually a converted church). Also there was a sidebar witj mechanics for a practice the young vampires apparently call cow tipping - sneaking out to fields to feed on cows. In a story set in Denver. One of the 20 most populated cities in the country.<br /> <br /> Hunting Ground: the Rockies was much better overall, although it still missed on a few points, like getting the location of the Pearl Street mall wrong, and having Max Roman own a skyscraper that doesn't actually exist but is still mentioned to be one of the biggest in the city. When there's a perfectly good 1st Bank building, which is actually one of tallest in the city, and is probably the most distinctive part of Denver's skyline and sort of looks like a bird's beak. But I forgive those missteps because it gets more right than it gets wrong.<br /> <br /> I'm also pretty used to fictional stories set in Colorado just completely making up specific locations. Like The Last of Us - there is no University of Eastern Colorado (nor do any of the game's locations actually exist). Community - there is no Greendale Comminity College (and no Greendale). Often Colorado just ends up being a name to put to generic mountainous settings.<br /> <br /> Anyway, sorry for the tangent. Point is, yeah, when fiction you like is set in a place you know well, it's exciting to see the points they get right and disappointing to see the parts they get wrong. Thorough research goes a long way.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, how many cities on the front range are actually worth the time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T22:45:19-08:00","id":1015555,"title":"","content":"If you're planning to feature Cairo in a game, remember that this exists:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\"> Lonely Together &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I know that I completely forgot, so I bet other people did too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T23:27:58-08:00","id":1015572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015489#post1015489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this how people living elsewhere always feel when their cities are visited in roleplaying?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Demon's version of Sydney the Aboriginal in the art looked more like a native American than a native Australian which is abit disappointing and cane toads aren't really a NSW thing unless you're really far north, but other than that it was rather good and incorporated a tonne of aussie culture without it being a stereotype or caricature (even used &quot;Every australian animal is weird and out to murder you&quot; in it without it being ridiculous). Beast's Adelaide was abit weird, it's a cool little setting but it doesn't really have anything in it that sticks out as australian aside from the Bunyip. I have no idea how accurate Werewolf Alice Springs is, but I liked the large scope history for australian werewolves (Kurditcha were a nice touch).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 12-11-2016, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T07:18:10-08:00","id":1015666,"title":"","content":"No Halifax, but Montreal and Toronto have been featured several times each, with differing results. Wasn't a fan of the 1st ed Toronto in the Chroniclers Guide, its focus on Old Money Toronto seems to forget that Toronto was a tiny frontier outpost until pretty late. Changeling 2es Toronto looks like it'll be better, and hit the actual self-conception of the city a little better, although I worry that it'll be pretty much the positive self-conception without really getting the huge divisions within the city. <br /> <br /> Montreal was a pretty unique setting in VtR2e. Not sure how well it really reflected the city though, it seems like you could replace the rules around Mount Royal and the cross with any similar monument or landmark and the setting could be ported to almost any city, so long as you can find a similar group to take the role the native vampires play in Montreal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T07:25:32-08:00","id":1015667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015666#post1015666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Montreal was a pretty unique setting in VtR2e. Not sure how well it really reflected the city though, it seems like you could replace the rules around Mount Royal and the cross with any similar monument or landmark and the setting could be ported to almost any city, so long as you can find a similar group to take the role the native vampires play in Montreal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah theres not much in the setting that is particular about montreal. Additionnaly i disliked the whole theban miracles dont work and there isnt a big presence of the lancea. This doesnt seem to take into account the huge presence that the church has in the history of montreal.<br /> <br /> Now dont misunderstand. I find the pit of the nameless to be an interesting concept. But i'll just put it in another city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T18:35:00-08:00","id":1015929,"title":"","content":"I mean, they call Montreal the City of a Thousand Steeples. The fact that most of the steeples now mount converted lofts and art spaces and such-like is just another bit of Quebec-specific feeling you can impart; an intensely religious culture that, all of a sudden, dropped their religiousity en masse, with the massive social upheaval that involves, now settled as a secular society surrounded by symbols of their past. Now, you COULD have collapsed the Lance with that, if you have the Lance be massively dominant before the Nameless to a ridiculous degree, such that the surviving vampires constantly come across reminders of the Sanctum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T16:18:02-08:00","id":1016790,"title":"","content":"Having worked through most of the book, I'm surprised to say that my least-favorite Covenant (the Carthians) had my favorite chapter. I loved how it danced around the globe and showed us new domains, and how they all differ; Hanoi jumped off the page and demands to be played yesterday. Are the Long Lo Suoi supposed to be what the Union might look like abroad? I dig it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:11:13-08:00","id":1016817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1015489#post1015489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this how people living elsewhere always feel when their cities are visited in roleplaying?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I've ever seen a take on LA or Orange County that I've really liked. Those places are so deeply interesting to me, but nothing that makes them interesting to me ever seems to make it into game stuff. <br /> <br /> And Tokyo, I don't really see much treatment of in games. When I do, it's generally very over-the-top goofy or whatever. So likewise, it never hits on the little stuff that makes Tokyo my favorite city in the world. <br /> <br /> That said, I've lived all over. But I tended to live in places that get ignored or grossly misrepresented in games (read: poor and non-white neighborhoods). So, again, usually not too keen on that stuff. <br /> <br /> Honestly, one of the reasons Damnation City is one of my all-time favorite game books is that it hits on some of that stuff, while not being specific enough that it can feel wrong. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1016790#post1016790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having worked through most of the book, I'm surprised to say that my least-favorite Covenant (the Carthians) had my favorite chapter. I loved how it danced around the globe and showed us new domains, and how they all differ; Hanoi jumped off the page and demands to be played yesterday. Are the Long Lo Suoi supposed to be what the Union might look like abroad? I dig it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That was kind of what I wanted them to be, in really simple terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:18:28-08:00","id":1016823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1016817#post1016817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I've ever seen a take on LA or Orange County that I've really liked. Those places are so deeply interesting to me, but nothing that makes them interesting to me ever seems to make it into game stuff. <br /> <br /> And Tokyo, I don't really see much treatment of in games. When I do, it's generally very over-the-top goofy or whatever. So likewise, it never hits on the little stuff that makes Tokyo my favorite city in the world. <br /> <br /> That said, I've lived all over. But I tended to live in places that get ignored or grossly misrepresented in games (read: poor and non-white neighborhoods). So, again, usually not too keen on that stuff. <br /> <br /> Honestly, one of the reasons Damnation City is one of my all-time favorite game books is that it hits on some of that stuff, while not being specific enough that it can feel wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always funny to me when prople treat LA as some sort of glittering metropolis for the ultra-elite; I don't think I've ever met a Californian from outside the city who didn't think of it as kind of a hellhole. If anything, it's more about having damn near every ethnicity you can imagine trying to make a living for themselves more than movie stars, but you never see that in pop culture.<br /> <br /> San Diego is weird. If it has any touchstones, it's the Navy and the Mexican and Japanese communities, with tourism and the university close behind, which is why I kinda balked at having a weird Occupy narrative - turned - armed militia thing pop up there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes. That was kind of what I wanted them to be, in really simple terms. </div> </div> </div>I know there's been some chatting about how archetypical Hunter groups change according to local flavor across the globe, so that was fun to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:31:01-08:00","id":1016830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1016817#post1016817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, one of the reasons Damnation City is one of my all-time favorite game books is that it hits on some of that stuff, while not being specific enough that it can feel wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>A great deal of the location work in <i>Damnation City</i> is true stuff from DC. A place that I live that isn't well-treated in RPGs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:32:42-08:00","id":1016832,"title":"","content":"I was born in, and worked in and around Philly for a while, and I often found myself driving home up Kelly Drive, which follows the Schuykill River past both Fairmount Park <i>and </i>Laurel Hill Cemetery. I'm very pleased that Laurel Hill Cemetery got a shout-out, part of it is built on cliffs, and you see mausoleums built into sides of cliffs and looming up above you on top of them, it is gothic as hell. I'm very glad that both Fairmount and Laurel Hill got shout-outs in the setting write-up in Beast. <br /> <br /> Hell, there's a several mile stretch along the Schuykill that could be one huge Elysium: the Basilica of Saints Peter and Paul, the Art Museum, Fairmount Park, Boathouse Row, the Philly Zoo, Laurel Hill Cemetery... There are enough locations that every Covenant could have their own area along the Schuykill, and that could make politics very interesting in Philly. Anybody who wants to do a chronicle in Philly, you would be doing yourself a grave disservice if you did not use those locations; if you are doing a chronicle in Philly and are not including those locations, then you are quite frankly <i>not doing it right. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:49:51-08:00","id":1016838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1016832#post1016832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was born in, and worked in and around Philly for a while, and I often found myself driving home up Kelly Drive, which follows the Schuykill River past both Fairmount Park <i>and </i>Laurel Hill Cemetery. I'm very pleased that Laurel Hill Cemetery got a shout-out, part of it is built on cliffs, and you see mausoleums built into sides of cliffs and looming up above you on top of them, it is gothic as hell. I'm very glad that both Fairmount and Laurel Hill got shout-outs in the setting write-up in Beast.<br /> <br /> Hell, there's a several mile stretch along the Schuykill that could be one huge Elysium: the Basilica of Saints Peter and Paul, the Art Museum, Fairmount Park, Boathouse Row, the Philly Zoo, Laurel Hill Cemetery... There are enough locations that every Covenant could have their own area along the Schuykill, and that could make politics very interesting in Philly. Anybody who wants to do a chronicle in Philly, you would be doing yourself a grave disservice if you did not use those locations; if you are doing a chronicle in Philly and are not including those locations, then you are quite frankly <i>not doing it right. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Chuck Wendig was from the Philly region (about an hour or so north of it) when he developed Hunter. It's partly why Philly is the signature city for Vigil. I was actually living in Philly at the time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1016823#post1016823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's always funny to me when prople treat LA as some sort of glittering metropolis for the ultra-elite; I don't think I've ever met a Californian from outside the city who didn't think of it as kind of a hellhole. If anything, it's more about having damn near every ethnicity you can imagine trying to make a living for themselves more than movie stars, but you never see that in pop culture.<br /> <br /> I know there's been some chatting about how archetypical Hunter groups change according to local flavor across the globe, so that was fun to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. LA is ridiculously diverse. But you never see that in the Whedonesque &quot;the blonde white girl might maybe have a black friend&quot; perception of Los Angeles. I grew up in South Central LA. There was no glamour. I was the only white kid in my school. You don't see that LA in games, unless it's some strange Straight Outta Compton pastiche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T18:18:34-08:00","id":1016849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1016838#post1016838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chuck Wendig was from the Philly region (about an hour or so north of it) when he developed Hunter. It's partly why Philly is the signature city for Vigil. I was actually living in Philly at the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yep. LA is ridiculously diverse. But you never see that in the Whedonesque &quot;the blonde white girl might maybe have a black friend&quot; perception of Los Angeles. I grew up in South Central LA. There was no glamour. I was the only white kid in my school. You don't see that LA in games, unless it's some strange Straight Outta Compton pastiche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that explains the shout-out to Hunters ruling Fairmount Park in Beast. I know very little about LA, but even just browsing the Wiki article, it's an absurdly diverse city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T01:00:24-08:00","id":1016937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1016817#post1016817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, one of the reasons Damnation City is one of my all-time favorite game books is that it hits on some of that stuff, while not being specific enough that it can feel wrong.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that the blurb on Amsterdam is workable, I am ever disappointed that the rest of the world views my country through the lens of that one city. The place is like an amusement park. There are places with so much more potential than just: red-light districts and massive amounts of tourists, whoop whoop easy Herds... There are hookers and drug-tourists everywhere here. Rotterdam is way grittier and more interesting to international trade than Amsterdam is. The Hague is where the actual politics take place, despite it not being the capitol-city it is where the government resides. Maastricht and Nijmegen are two of the oldest cities in Europe, they go back to Roman times. The country-side province of Brabant is <i>the</i> XTC-producer of the world.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:25:53-08:00","id":1017263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1016838#post1016838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chuck Wendig was from the Philly region (about an hour or so north of it) when he developed Hunter. It's partly why Philly is the signature city for Vigil. I was actually living in Philly at the time. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yep. LA is ridiculously diverse. But you never see that in the Whedonesque &quot;the blonde white girl might maybe have a black friend&quot; perception of Los Angeles. I grew up in South Central LA. There was no glamour. I was the only white kid in my school. You don't see that LA in games, unless it's some strange Straight Outta Compton pastiche.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think most peoples perceptions of LA begin and end at Hollywood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T15:45:03-08:00","id":1017360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1017263#post1017263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think most peoples perceptions of LA begin and end at Hollywood.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's so sad. That's such a small portion of LA by population, and it's like... nothing of what makes it interesting. If you start in Hollywood and walk outward, you don't find anything interesting until you get to Oki Dog in Fairfax. Hollywood hasn't been cool since Raymond Chandler was writing about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T23:14:21-08:00","id":1017510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1017360#post1017360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's so sad. That's such a small portion of LA by population, and it's like... nothing of what makes it interesting. If you start in Hollywood and walk outward, you don't find anything interesting until you get to Oki Dog in Fairfax. Hollywood hasn't been cool since Raymond Chandler was writing about it.</div> </div> </div> </div> No doubt that there is alot more to LA then Hollywood, but Hollywood is what has the global cultural influence, not the rest of LA.<br /> <br /> Like there is alot more to the GTA then Downtown Toronto, but most people outside the GTA think about Toronto, they're thinking about downtown Toronto with the CN Tower, Skydome, ect...<br /> <br /> Its just the way it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T00:44:10-08:00","id":1017530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1017510#post1017510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No doubt that there is alot more to LA then Hollywood, but Hollywood is what has the global cultural influence, not the rest of LA.<br /> ...<br /> Its just the way it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's just the way it is&quot; is never really a good way to rebut an opinion. Particularly when that opinion is &quot;a bunch of non-white, non-wealthy people get erased and that's not okay.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T03:01:37-08:00","id":1017562,"title":"","content":"Are there any other metaplot goodies besides the final fate of Prince Vidal?<br /> <br /> Yossarian: What Easter egg? Are you talking about the Sabbat reference in ToL?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T08:30:55-08:00","id":1017665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1017562#post1017562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any other metaplot goodies besides the final fate of Prince Vidal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you define &quot;metaplot&quot; in the context of Requiem, but if you mean recognizable characters and locations that have ongoing stories there are (probably missing some)...<ul><li>Some implications about the actual relation between the fallen Camarilla and the Invictus</li> <li>More current and ongoing info about some of the locations that were detailed in the VtR 2e Core</li> <li>A bit more Frances Black (Mekhet Clanbook)</li> <li>A bit Solomon Birch (not much) and details of Scratch's history (also a major Chicago character)</li> <li>More about the Burlesque Grotesque</li> <li>The Invictus &quot;Future Panel&quot; which might be picked up again later</li> <li>Lots of new characters that might be picked up again in future supplements</li> <li>Some other whack Sanctified and Dragon mysteries which may be played with later</li> </ul><br /> <b>Edit</b>: Speaking of Chicago, if you are interested in ongoing stories in the Requiem setting, I recommend picking up the original Requiem novels (A Hunger Like Fire; Blood In, Blood Out; Marriage of Virtue and Viciousness), Danse Macabre and the Strix Fiction Anthology. All are about our favourite Chicago licks and cover quite a span of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 12-15-2016, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T10:35:19-08:00","id":1017708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1016937#post1016937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that the blurb on Amsterdam is workable, I am ever disappointed that the rest of the world views my country through the lens of that one city. The place is like an amusement park. There are places with so much more potential than just: red-light districts and massive amounts of tourists, whoop whoop easy Herds... There are hookers and drug-tourists everywhere here. Rotterdam is way grittier and more interesting to international trade than Amsterdam is. The Hague is where the actual politics take place, despite it not being the capitol-city it is where the government resides. Maastricht and Nijmegen are two of the oldest cities in Europe, they go back to Roman times. The country-side province of Brabant is <i>the</i> XTC-producer of the world.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, when I think &quot;Amsterdam,&quot; I think drug tourism, legal prostitution, red light district and otherwise. The drug tourism thing I know from all the stoner comedies set there and the obligatory &quot;legal weed&quot; joke in any American movie set there. I'm sure there's more to it than that, but those are what springs to mind when I think about the city.<br /> <br /> Rotterdam sounds like it's far more grim than Amsterdam, but that may be because the international news stories I here about it are Jewish citizens being told to keep a low profile and even leaving the city due to harassment by the usual suspects and Muslim immigrants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T13:02:58-08:00","id":1017767,"title":"","content":"How effective are the Lancea's anti-sorcery fighting merits? Considering how much time an acolite needs to pull a ritual, I assumed they were performed outside combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T16:34:37-08:00","id":1017847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1017767#post1017767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How effective are the Lancea's anti-sorcery fighting merits? Considering how much time an acolite needs to pull a ritual, I assumed they were performed outside combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>They work on non-Cruac forms of magic too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T16:48:57-08:00","id":1017850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1017562#post1017562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any other metaplot goodies besides the final fate of Prince Vidal?<br /> <br /> Yossarian: What Easter egg? Are you talking about the Sabbat reference in ToL?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the missing passages after Eschaton 7:7","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T01:43:10-08:00","id":1017999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1017708#post1017708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, when I think &quot;Amsterdam,&quot; I think drug tourism, legal prostitution, red light district and otherwise. The drug tourism thing I know from all the stoner comedies set there and the obligatory &quot;legal weed&quot; joke in any American movie set there. I'm sure there's more to it than that, but those are what springs to mind when I think about the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point being that prostitution and drugs aren't hard to come by anywhere in this country. The only thing that makes Amsterdam unique is the absolutely inhuman amounts of tourists the city attracts, because foreigners are raised with the idea that it is it's own indipendent state or some shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rotterdam sounds like it's far more grim than Amsterdam, but that may be because the international news stories I here about it are Jewish citizens being told to keep a low profile and even leaving the city due to harassment by the usual suspects and Muslim immigrants. </div> </div> </div>I fear you've been misinformed. Rotterdam is one of the most successfull multi-cultural cities in the country. (The mayor's even a Moroccan.) Always has been. Having a fuck-off big international harbor does that to your population's mentality. That harbor is also one of the reasons why the place is more gritty, that and the fact that it is close-by to the aforementioned XTC-province, Brabant. Lots of international drug trades going on. It's true that many of our ISIS recruits have come from places in South Holland (the province where Rotterdam is located too). But they hail from places like Zoetermeer and the &quot;projects&quot; in Delft.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T04:45:25-08:00","id":1018024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1017999#post1017999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point being that prostitution and drugs aren't hard to come by anywhere in this country. The only thing that makes Amsterdam unique is the absolutely inhuman amounts of tourists the city attracts, because foreigners are raised with the idea that it is it's own indipendent state or some shit.<br /> <br /> <br /> I fear you've been misinformed. Rotterdam is one of the most successfull multi-cultural cities in the country. (The mayor's even a Moroccan.) Always has been. Having a fuck-off big international harbor does that to your population's mentality. That harbor is also one of the reasons why the place is more gritty, that and the fact that it is close-by to the aforementioned XTC-province, Brabant. Lots of international drug trades going on. It's true that many of our ISIS recruits have come from places in South Holland (the province where Rotterdam is located too). But they hail from places like Zoetermeer and the &quot;projects&quot; in Delft.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, my apologies then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T22:08:01-08:00","id":1019613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1014495#post1014495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was just saying the same thing. Definitely not a fan of the art within. Too much photoshop slathered onto actual pictures. Not my kind of &quot;art.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>CofD is not my main interest (although, given time, I'll read this book, because I like fluff and am curious what direction they took) from the lines currently under OP's nurturing, but since it could be applied through most of them, I want to join Larry in this.<br /> <br /> I don't intend this as a bashing on anyone, or anyone's work. It's not about the quality of the artworks in the books, basically since V20, but the style. It's also not about WoD vs. CofD, since a lot of the 1e NWoD books were among my favorites, artistic wise, Changeling and Vampire particularly. I know personal tastes, are, duh, personal and if the writers, developers, art director or anyone who are making the calls like the photography-styled artworks better, that's their choice. I just know, that I liked the old CWoD books' sketchy b&amp;w the most, but a lot of the NWoD 1e books were also very catching with the line-thematic monocolors and penlines. The CofD 2e book was also good (and not just because of the re-used arts) and Dark Eras too. Also, those old and mentioned newer books were conveyed a very unique, &quot;WW book&quot; feel, which I feel the new books are lacking, because there are too much different styles of artworks in them, regardless of quality.<br /> <br /> I know, aside from personal tastes, nowadays full-color is usually deemed as a step-up in quality (a notion I honestly cannot comprehend) and I'd bet that just as many (or at least enough to justify it) people likes the current direction than not. Still, I do and will mourn the look of the old books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 12-20-2016, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T09:43:09-08:00","id":1019825,"title":"","content":"So long as all of the &quot;Photographs with photoshop slathered onto them&quot; are done by Samuel Araya, I don't mind in the slightest. Mummy is my favorite gameline, and a big part of that is Sam's artwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:06:02-08:00","id":1019857,"title":"","content":"I just got the book and I want to love it, but the cursive fonts in a large number of the documents continue to make me struggle. The fonts were the one thing about the clanbooks that I loathed because it makes it so hard to actually read what's written without copy-pasting the text onto a notepad file first. Otherwise my enjoyment dwindles beneath the effort of deciphering what the text is actually saying.<br /> <br /> I'll comment again when I've gotten over this hurdle and can actually comment on the quality of the writing itself instead of the difficulties I'm having with its presentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T19:12:35-08:00","id":1020124,"title":"","content":"I feel foolish, what exactly was the fate of Vidal, other than writing his confession to who he wrote it to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:15:01-08:00","id":1020300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1019857#post1019857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got the book and I want to love it, but the cursive fonts in a large number of the documents continue to make me struggle. The fonts were the one thing about the clanbooks that I loathed because it makes it so hard to actually read what's written without copy-pasting the text onto a notepad file first. Otherwise my enjoyment dwindles beneath the effort of deciphering what the text is actually saying.<br /> <br /> I'll comment again when I've gotten over this hurdle and can actually comment on the quality of the writing itself instead of the difficulties I'm having with its presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree there. Ive had to copy paste into docs or notepad to read many of them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T06:28:24-08:00","id":1020346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1017767#post1017767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How effective are the Lancea's anti-sorcery fighting merits? Considering how much time an acolite needs to pull a ritual, I assumed they were performed outside combat.</div> </div> </div> </div> You call them anti-sorcery merits... but they do say &quot;any magic&quot; or &quot;magical effects&quot; in the actual rules. So, that leads me to believe that Sorcerous Eunuch and Shield Against Sorcery equally apply against Dominate and Nightmare as they do against something like Gorgon's Gaze. <br /> <br /> Silence is potentially effective against Dominate or other social powers of vampires. While you can still Charm someone using Majesty, its harder to direct your followers when you can't talk. The problem comes down to healing the wounds or just flat out resisting them through Resilience. The most likely canidate for using Silence against (Ventrue) tend to also have lots of Resilience. On the other hand? If your target is wearing armor? Throats are often unprotected, so this is like having a free called shot to deal damage without penalty, and that's pretty neat. Against the living, without magical healing, we could be talking about a killing strike as they choke to death. <br /> <br /> A Hammer Against Witches is the only power I can see that actually involves interacting with ritual sorceries of some kind. Barring crossover, blood magics are the only powers that currently use Extended Actions to invoke. This is pretty much the weak link, considering that interrupting rituals tend to be pretty rare in my experience. Maybe at the cumulation of a plot, or an opening of a war. But, in my experience, very few rituals happen where they can be interrupted.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the first ability in the biggest advantage. Being able to subtract 3 dice from any magic power that targets anyone around you is pretty awesome. No matter what the other two can do, you still want all three dots just for the full ability of Shield Against Sorcery. So, I consider 2 &amp; 3 to be just bonuses to begin with. Silence has some nifty benefits that, while still situational, come up often enough and have enough impact that its still more than worthwhile on its own merits. HAW is entirely ST dependant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:00:40-08:00","id":1020580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020346#post1020346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You call them anti-sorcery merits... but they do say &quot;any magic&quot; or &quot;magical effects&quot; in the actual rules. So, that leads me to believe that Sorcerous Eunuch and Shield Against Sorcery equally apply against Dominate and Nightmare as they do against something like Gorgon's Gaze.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Any magical effect&quot; is not the same as &quot;any supernatural effect,&quot; dominate and nightmare have never been magical. Barring threnodies, only the blood sorceries are magical.<br /> <br /> And if one expands what is or is not a magical effect, then that applies to all aspects of the merits, not just the beneficial ones. <br /> <br /> So someone who has sorcerous eunuch would be incapable of using any discipline that their magical immunity provides protection against, that's the logic of the merit- give up magic to gain protection against magic. <br /> <br /> Likewise, Shield against Sorcery applies indiscriminately to everyone within willpower yard- Including people the character is trying to use their disciplines on, or anyone that their friends wants to use a discipline on in willpower yards. <br /> <br /> So in point of fact expanding their use like that would make those merits less useful, not more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:32:43-08:00","id":1020608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020124#post1020124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel foolish, what exactly was the fate of Vidal, other than writing his confession to who he wrote it to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you on that. Unless it's just the revelation that he survived Katrina or there is something in the Ordo chapter I haven't yet read, nothing seems to suggest to me this is Vidal's &quot;final fate.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T17:44:13-08:00","id":1020728,"title":"","content":"Then we need a more useful definition of what is and is not &quot;magic,&quot; particularly when it comes to other splats. Are numeb magic? Are contracts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T05:27:11-08:00","id":1020829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020580#post1020580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Any magical effect&quot; is not the same as &quot;any supernatural effect,&quot; dominate and nightmare have never been magical.</div> </div> </div> </div> I call BS. In fact, I see several references to Dominate's ability to supress memory as &quot;magic&quot; in the discipline section. Disciplines are both magic and supernatural.<br /> <br /> You are possibly getting confused with terms like &quot;spells,&quot; &quot;ritual magic&quot; and &quot;ceremonial magic,&quot; all of which do refer to abilities distinct from the standard Disciplines. We could call a theban sorcery ritual a spell and get away with it. We could not call Dominate a spell or ritual magic and be correct.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So someone who has sorcerous eunuch would be incapable of using any discipline that their magical immunity provides protection against, that's the logic of the merit- give up magic to gain protection against magic. </div> </div> </div> If you read the actual merit, Sorcerous Eunuch specifically says that they can't learn Cruac, Theban or any other blood sorceries. Its clear that S.E. only forbids ritual sorceries and doesn't forbid other kinds of magic. You're giving up specific kinds of magic for general protection against other kinds of magic.<br /> <br /> In fact, going strictly by the rules, a Sorcerous Eunuch can learn Coils, Oaths and the Law - none of those three are listed under the Blood Sorcery section of the core book - they're clearly something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise, Shield against Sorcery applies indiscriminately to everyone within willpower yard- Including people the character is trying to use their disciplines on, or anyone that their friends wants to use a discipline on in willpower yards. </div> </div> </div> That is true. However, if you're using Shield Against Sorcery, you're holding a weapon, very likely with the intent to use it. Vigor, Celerity and Resilience are unaffected by Shield Against Sorcery. Crusaders are well aware of their own drawbacks and train appropriately. In fact, its also notable that, unlike Gaze of the Gorgon, the Theban attack spell Apparation of the Host doesn't use any rolls in the middle of combat, making it also unaffected by Shield Against Sorcery.<br /> <br /> If, for some reason, you wanted to use your own magical abilities without Shield Against Sorcery interfering, you can also just put away your weapon, which removes the penalty. Quick Draw is your friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-22-2016, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T05:52:14-08:00","id":1020842,"title":"","content":"It really would be nice if the Devs could decide in a final matter on what's 'magic' for the purposes of different abilities that mention magic specifically, so arguments like this needn't happen all the time (they were even more common in 1e)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T06:30:47-08:00","id":1020850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020728#post1020728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then we need a more useful definition of what is and is not &quot;magic,&quot; particularly when it comes to other splats. Are numeb magic? Are contracts?</div> </div> </div> </div> Werewolf Gifts, fetishes and rites are all listed as under the Spirit Magic heading; Dread Powers of the prey are called magic as well. Changeling uses the term &quot;magic' to refer to lots of things, including Contracts, tokens, hedgespun, and the Mask. Pretty much everything a mage does is magic of some kind. Beast Lairs are called magical, and Atavisms occasionally refer to other Atavisms as &quot;magical effects.&quot; The Divine Fire allows Prometheans to perform their &quot;magic,&quot; but no word on what those magics officially are - one would presume Transmutations at least, and forging the soul absolutely is considered magic. Demon the Descent calls their Embeds / Exploits magical powers, and refers to the powers of angels as &quot;magical powers granted by the God Machine.&quot; Core CofD book refers to Numina as &quot;discrete magical powers.&quot; <br /> <br /> The simple truth is that &quot;magic&quot; and &quot;supernatural&quot; are used interchangably in the books; which term being used seems to depend more on what kind of feeling that the writers are going for at any given time than anything else. A little sidebar about Supernatural Tolerance in the CofD core even refers to anything that Blood Potency is used to resist as &quot;magical powers.&quot; I think that the main reason that the anti-magic merits in the LeS section use the word &quot;magic&quot; is simply because the writer was trying to provoke an old school Catholic witch-hunter vibe while keeping the merit open ended. &quot;Magic,&quot; in Catholic circles, is a dirty term to refer to any non-Christian (or Christian-based demonic) supernatural effect, while miracle refers to Christian-style supernatural effect that comes from their God or related divine beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T07:56:27-08:00","id":1020880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020728#post1020728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then we need a more useful definition of what is and is not &quot;magic,&quot; particularly when it comes to other splats. Are numeb magic? Are contracts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What MCN said. Essentially &quot;supernatural&quot; == &quot;magic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T10:36:07-08:00","id":1020941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020880#post1020880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What MCN said. Essentially &quot;supernatural&quot; == &quot;magic&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No way I'm letting a one-point merit give people not interested in Cruac/Theban a three+ point resistance to every supernatural effect in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your character has been subject to a series of terrifying rituals and experiments, which affords him a <i><b>near immunity to sorcery</b></i>. Any dice pool for a magical effect targeting your character suffers his Resolve as a penalty. </div> </div> </div>I don't think it takes much of a leap of logic to understand this merit resists Sorcery Powers, not every discipline, devotion, ability or effect with any hint of supernaturality and a dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T10:42:50-08:00","id":1020942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020941#post1020941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No way I'm letting a one-point merit give people not interested in Cruac/Theban a three+ point resistance to every supernatural effect in the game.<br /> <br /> I don't think it takes much of a leap of logic to understand this merit resists Sorcery Powers, not every discipline, devotion, ability or effect with any hint of supernaturality and a dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like we agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T10:46:09-08:00","id":1020944,"title":"","content":"The character would also be unable to learn blood sorcery. That implies blood sorcery (among the vampiric powers) is what's affected. (I don't want to say resisted since it reduces successes, not dice, like an armor against sorcery.)<br /> How it affects other types of magic that vampires cannot learn is up to the ST, just like many other matters dealing with crossovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T10:49:43-08:00","id":1020945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020942#post1020942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like we agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. And of course, every table can interpret how they wish. But do you have any sort of justification for why this merit should lessen every stripe of discipline beyond the writers being loose with terminology occasionally?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T12:11:28-08:00","id":1020966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020945#post1020945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. And of course, every table can interpret how they wish. But do you have any sort of justification for why this merit should lessen every stripe of discipline beyond the writers being loose with terminology occasionally?</div> </div> </div> </div>This looks like a pretty simple RAW interpretation to me. It blanket works on magic. Now was there some intent that it should only apply to blood sorcery and theurgy like Cruac and Theban Sorcery? Maybe. But it's not clear from the text and I don't see a firm enough foundation for a RAI interpretation here.<br /> <br /> All that said, am I likely to house rule hack it to apply as I want? Yes, yes I am. Because you're right. Either its way too cheap a merit for what it does or someone just wrote sloppy rules. But as it stands I see no justification not to read it as its written.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I might note also that the prereqs for Crusade level 1 are relatively high, you basically have to build your character around the style, and Sorcerous Eunuch disallows you from ever learning Theban Sorcery, which in my opinion makes it a poor choice for Lancea characters unless they want to go the full witch-hunting crusader route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 12-22-2016, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T12:23:42-08:00","id":1020970,"title":"","content":"If you think it needs to be reworded there's a thread for that kind of thing. This is still the editing process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T13:08:21-08:00","id":1020984,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty obvious that it wasn't intended to work on any and all supernatural powers. Likely, &quot;magic&quot; was meant to refer to the sort done by ritual - Blood Sorcery, Wolf and Pack Rites, Awakened Spells, etc. Granted, that's not explicitly stated, and I would wager that's an intentional choice. I kind of doubt David was interested in getting into the semantics of whether supernatural abiliy X counts as &quot;magic&quot; or not. Nor do I expect he felt like setting a prescedent for crossover by saying &quot;these specific powers that these splats use are magic and these specific powers aren't.&quot; Nor do I expect he had the wordcount to do so even if he wanted to. This is CofD, guys; natural language abounds, interpretation requires personal judgment and good faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-22-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T14:26:53-08:00","id":1021008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020970#post1020970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think it needs to be reworded there's a thread for that kind of thing. This is still the editing process.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will make the suggestion. Among other things the experiences needed for 2 dots of Theban Sorcery are 8 times greater than those needed for Sorcerous Eunuch. It also isn't clear if the effects of Sorcerous Eunuch and Shield Against Magic stack (I assume not).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually the errata thread is closed. I do agree that the most likely case is intent that Sorcerous Eunuch is intended for ritualized magic (and the addition of just that one natural language word clarifies the semantic content of the sentence masterfully). A bigger problem is in the pre-reqs for the Crusade merit where the Sorcerous Eunuch merit is equated to 2 dots of Theban Sorcery. One costs 1 experience while the other costs 8 experiences. That looks like a math fail. Also of the three Crusade maneuvers Shield Against Sorcery is arguably the most powerful. In my games I'll be using the following hacks.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sorcerous Eunuch </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(4): Resolve 3 &amp; Lancea et Sanctum Status 1 {Note that this Merit only applies to blood sorcery, theurgy, and other ritualized spellcasting (e.g. Cr\u00faac, Theban Sorcery, Rites, Arcane Spells, etc.)}</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crusade [Style] (1~3): Resolve 3, Occult 2, Weaponry 2, Lancea et Sanctum Status 1, &amp; either Theban Sorcery 1 or Sorcerous Eunuch {Note: the proper order for this merit\u2019s maneuvers is: Silence (1), A Hammer Against Witches (2), Shield Against Sorcery (3); Note that Shield Against Sorcery works against all forms of supernatural \u201cmagic\u201d including Disciplines, Devotions, Embeds, Exploits, Gifts, Rites, etc. If the Vampire also has the Sorcerous Eunuch merit then she applies the higher of the two penalties to ritualized magic forms (e.g., Cr\u00faac, Theban Sorcery, Rites, Arcane Spells).} </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 12-22-2016, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:07:25-08:00","id":1021029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020984#post1020984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's pretty obvious that it wasn't intended to work on any and all supernatural powers. Likely, &quot;magic&quot; was meant to refer to the sort done by ritual - Blood Sorcery, Wolf and Pack Rites, Awakened Spells, etc. Granted, that's not explicitly stated, and I would wager that's an intentional choice. I kind of doubt David was interested in getting into the semantics of whether supernatural abiliy X counts as &quot;magic&quot; or not. Nor do I expect he felt like setting a prescedent for crossover by saying &quot;these specific powers that these splats use are magic and these specific powers don't.&quot; Nor do I expect he had the wordcount to do so even if he wanted to. This is CofD, guys; natural language abounds, interpretation requires personal judgment and good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. <br /> <br /> I could have technically used more than that entire chapter's word count sussing out what a single trait does and doesn't apply to, and there would still be questions. <br /> <br /> Your interpretation is a pretty solid one here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:27:27-08:00","id":1021039,"title":"","content":"I feel like a good stand-in is all supernatural extended actions and all things where being &quot;magic&quot; is important to the thematics, at the ST's discression. I.e. Mage, Hedge Magicians, Alchemists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:57:20-08:00","id":1021056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1021039#post1021039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like a good stand-in is all supernatural extended actions and all things where being &quot;magic&quot; is important to the thematics, at the ST's discression. I.e. Mage, Hedge Magicians, Alchemists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I wouldn't say that's a bad metric either. Although there's some room for debate with some things like Hunter Endowments and stuff. <br /> <br /> Which I like. I personally like a bit of fiat and unpredictability with magic. I prefer players (and by extension, characters) to not always know exactly how things are going to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:57:54-08:00","id":1021057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1020829#post1020829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I call BS. In fact, I see several references to Dominate's ability to supress memory as &quot;magic&quot; in the discipline section. Disciplines are both magic and supernatural.<br /> <br /> You are possibly getting confused with terms like &quot;spells,&quot; &quot;ritual magic&quot; and &quot;ceremonial magic,&quot; all of which do refer to abilities distinct from the standard Disciplines. We could call a theban sorcery ritual a spell and get away with it. We could not call Dominate a spell or ritual magic and be correct.<br /> If you read the actual merit, Sorcerous Eunuch specifically says that they can't learn Cruac, Theban or any other blood sorceries. Its clear that S.E. only forbids ritual sorceries and doesn't forbid other kinds of magic. You're giving up specific kinds of magic for general protection against other kinds of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not confused about anything, thank you.<br /> <br /> When I read the merits, I noticed that literally both of them use sorcery as synonyms for magic, but then again so does the English language. &quot;A Null zone for sorcery,&quot; and &quot;near immunity to sorcery,&quot; are in the rules for the merits. <br /> <br /> And Sorcerous Eunuch, the name kind of gives it away, forbids the character from using sorcery, no &quot;theban, cruac, or other blood sorceries.&quot; <br /> <br /> So if other disciplines are magic, then they're sorceries, and not allowed to the sorcerous eunuch. <br /> <br /> But since I know that Vampire Second Edition literally defined disciplines as preternatural, that's not a problem for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T04:20:33-08:00","id":1021221,"title":"","content":"Umm.... that's not what's actually written, StSword. It literally lists &quot;Theban Sorcery, Cr\u00faac, or any other blood sorceries.&quot; That's a direct quote. Unlike &quot;magic,&quot; &quot;Blood Sorceries&quot; is an official term, as denoted by the title of the section that covers Cruac, Theban and other similar powers in the core book, separate from Coils or the clan disciplines. I'm sorry, but you are mistaken on this matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-23-2016, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T13:50:25-08:00","id":1022443,"title":"","content":"Edit: NVM got two people confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":".  Not relevant 12-26-2016, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T13:59:06-08:00","id":1022447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1022443#post1022443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But David Hill came in and basically said <i>you</i> were mistaken on this matter. Not directly - he told someone who stated the other position (that it applies to blood sorcery, mage stuff, spirit rites, etc) that she had it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think MCN and StSword are talking about Sorcerous Eunuch, whereas David and I were talking about Crusade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T14:05:41-08:00","id":1022448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1022447#post1022447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think MCN and StSword are talking about Sorcerous Eunuch, whereas David and I were talking about Crusade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Okay, post redacted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:31:59-08:00","id":1025956,"title":"","content":"So no clarification on Vidal? Phooey!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T14:59:37-08:00","id":1026177,"title":"","content":"I finally bought the book, awesome so far. <br /> <br /> But I still don't know know how say Cruac Void Creature gets vitae, does it feed like a, vampire, and how much vitae can it hold? <br /> <br /> Show I just use a Characters BP as if it was the Void Creatures or it's magnidude in place of BP for the Void Creature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T18:45:46-08:00","id":1026260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1025956#post1025956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no clarification on Vidal? Phooey!</div> </div> </div> </div>Vidal's current state is presented within the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T19:14:55-08:00","id":1026266,"title":"","content":"I just finished the book and while i like parts of it, is just me or Carthian law is not very well written/tested? <br /> <br /> For exampl Empower Judiciary says that the appointed judge can make a legal statement that will become law but at the same time said statement doesnt necesarily have to have anything to do with the law in question.<br /> <br /> Like the examples says a judge can proclaim &quot;None shall murder another Kindred&quot; which in truth enforces &quot;Jonathan Palmer is not allowed murdering; mortal or Kindred.&quot; which kind of garantees jonathan is gonna break this law because the proclamation didnt prohibit the killing of mortals. I am understanding this wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T19:47:26-08:00","id":1026279,"title":"","content":"The Chorister merit is the most generous. You gain a dot of Cruac and actress to CoC merits. This qualifies one for Cruac Styles. <br /> <br /> A Lances Sactum character with 5 dots of Theban Sorcery with the Chorister Merit and 1 Dot of Cruac can get the Void Cruac Style at 5 dots and the retainer merit at 5 dots to end up with a Void Creature that has 5 dots of Theban Sorcery. Weird, but interesting. <br /> <br /> An alliance between LS and CoC, might be rare, but scary when they find synergies between types of blood sorcery. <br /> <br /> Also the Cruac God can use parts form any formerily living thing, which can include Changelings, werewolves, stranger things. This spell is amoung the most powerful in the game, it'd make mages nervous. <br /> <br /> 25 vitea and it will have effective BP of 8, size 5, and 25 dots to split amoung attributes and Disciplines. Very flexible. There is a lot of things you can do with that. So many possiblies. If you have 5 dots of Cruac its not even hard to create by yourself. <br /> <br /> Primal Creation &amp; Unbridled Choas Styles we're buffed as well, combine the effects for some truly twisted shit. <br /> <br /> You can create new Supernatural Beings with Creations Cloning ability, Clone Changelings, Prommies, Fetches, Werewolves, Beasts, maybe stranger things like hobgoblins, Supernal Creatures, ect... <br /> <br /> I'm not sure how long the Protean effect of Unbridled Choas is supposed to last, but if permanent, it could lead to some freaky horrors. <br /> <br /> From the fiction, Choas and Creation are relatively natural, but Void isn't of the Dark Mother, it's creepy and dark and horrible even by Vampire Standards, maybe even something that would feel wrong to Beasts. <br /> <br /> The Fiction is really good so far, but the LS and CoC stories reminded me of the first heavy metal movie in the way they we're constructed. Or 1001 nights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T20:07:07-08:00","id":1026283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1026260#post1026260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vidal's current state is presented within the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read the entire Les section and unless I missed it, there is no explanation? I am embarasingly confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T20:15:44-08:00","id":1026286,"title":"","content":"You can't take other circle merits with Chorister. All merits in that section, including cruac styles, have the unspoken requirement of Status 1 [Circle of Crone].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T06:02:59-08:00","id":1026465,"title":"","content":"The problem with unspoken rules is that you can't really expect people to know about them.<br /> <br /> I want to point out that you don't automatically gain the first dot of Cr\u00faac. You gain access to it so you can buy it, if you manage to find a teacher who is willing to teach you. That last part is a great deal easier with the Merit, but also not something that is granted automatically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:52:28-08:00","id":1026519,"title":"","content":"It's not an unspoken rule. P181, 'Members of the Circle of the Crone have access to the following Merits. Unless otherwise noted, they have an additional prerequisite of Status (Circle of the Crone) \u2022 or higher.' Each Merits section begins with a statement like that for each covenant.<br /> <br /> Before someone gets up in arms about something sounds like it wouldn't require Covenant Status, 'With Storyteller discretion, some of the Merits may be used outside their respective covenants. For example, the Carthian Merit \u201cMobilize Outrage\u201d doesn\u2019t offer any hard reasons why it couldn\u2019t be used outside the Movement, or even by human characters. Its inclusion here reflects the fact that it\u2019s generally taught to Carthians, and is an important tool to the Movement. While the sections state that such Merits require a dot of Covenant Status, use your best judgment for your chronicles. In some cases, for example \u201cToss That Shit Right Back,\u201d it could apply for non-Kindred characters as well.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-04-2017, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:07:48-08:00","id":1026528,"title":"","content":"&quot;With a teacher, she may purchase the first dot of Cr\u00faac and additional rituals. She can also purchase Circle of the Crone Merits.&quot;<br /> <br /> The above is a direct quote from the Choister merit in the book, so yes they can in fact gain CoC merits with this merit and the first dot of Cruac and buy additional merits well. <br /> <br /> Weirdly I'm not certain you have to be a Vampire to take it, a Ghoul likely can, and if a Ghoul can, then the Ghoul can have stuff like a Cruac Style. <br /> <br /> Its be interesting if a Strix had the merit, I could see the Strix being the origin of the Void Style in imination of the other Kindred originated Cruac Styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:06:54-08:00","id":1026554,"title":"","content":"Carthian Merit Sellout can allow a Carthian Prince to Learn Cruac/Cruac Styles, Theban Sorcery, Coils of the Dragon, Invictus Oaths, Carthian Laws, ect..., its likely the most powerful single merit in the book, but at high cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:40:08-08:00","id":1026569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1026528#post1026528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weirdly I'm not certain you have to be a Vampire to take it, a Ghoul likely can, and if a Ghoul can, then the Ghoul can have stuff like a Cruac Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls can't sacrifice Vitae to empower the rituals. I think they can learn basic ones though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:07:07-08:00","id":1026582,"title":"","content":"One-dot rituals don't require sacrificing Vitae. So ghouls can use those. Any higher is off the table, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:05:09-08:00","id":1027237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1026283#post1026283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read the entire Les section and unless I missed it, there is no explanation? I am embarasingly confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>I almost missed it as well, but check page 141 and see who Vidal sent his confession to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:33:41-08:00","id":1027251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1026260#post1026260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vidal's current state is presented within the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>He seems to be quite mad... Mad as a Malkovian...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T17:17:38-08:00","id":1027357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1026582#post1026582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One-dot rituals don't require sacrificing Vitae. So ghouls can use those. Any higher is off the table, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> If the Ghoul has a vampire to bleed for it liquid vitae it can use the more powerful rituals, just as a, Strix would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T17:45:37-08:00","id":1027368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1027357#post1027357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Ghoul has a vampire to bleed for it liquid vitae it can use the more powerful rituals, just as a, Strix would.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we want to go by RAW, it says that Ghouls can't use Disciplines that require them to spill blood or feed it to others. It says nothing about it having to be their own blood. Just that they can't use it if it requires spilling it.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't allow it.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it seems unlikely that they'd learn Cruac at all. I don't imagine many Acolytes would be teaching it to Ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T20:16:09-08:00","id":1027395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1027368#post1027368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we want to go by RAW, it says that Ghouls can't use Disciplines that require them to spill blood or feed it to others. It says nothing about it having to be their own blood. Just that they can't use it if it requires spilling it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls just can't 'let out' Vitae the way vampires can. They can only bleed blood.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:33:20-08:00","id":1027592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1027368#post1027368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we want to go by RAW, it says that Ghouls can't use Disciplines that require them to spill blood or feed it to others. It says nothing about it having to be their own blood. Just that they can't use it if it requires spilling it.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't allow it.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it seems unlikely that they'd learn Cruac at all. I don't imagine many Acolytes would be teaching it to Ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:33:54-08:00","id":1027594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1027395#post1027395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghouls just can't 'let out' Vitae the way vampires can. They can only bleed blood.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good counter point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:54:08-08:00","id":1027612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1026177#post1026177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finally bought the book, awesome so far. <br /> <br /> But I still don't know know how say Cruac Void Creature gets vitae, does it feed like a, vampire, and how much vitae can it hold? <br /> <br /> Show I just use a Characters BP as if it was the Void Creatures or it's magnidude in place of BP for the Void Creature?</div> </div> </div> </div> This is till unanswered. I think I'll just use the use the Cruac Gods method of feeding and use magnitude as BP. <br /> <br /> Also interesting to note is the Cruac God doesn't appear to suffer Vampire Feeding restrictions, it can feed on any flesh it can inflict lethal damage on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-06-2017, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:17:48-08:00","id":1027675,"title":"","content":"Unnatural Affinity merit \u2022 , Void Creatures allows a Character to use the Void Creatures as an easily accessed food source, you never need to feed on humans again. But a who knows what the long term effects of that deit would be. <br /> <br /> A Cruac 5 Vampire could summon a 7 health Void Creature with a \u2022 cruac ritual, possibly several times per night when needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-06-2017, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T16:02:56-08:00","id":1027895,"title":"","content":"&quot;The products of Blood Sorcery can't be used to sustain life or even unlife&quot;<br /> 1st paragraph under &quot;Creation&quot; in Blood Sorcery pg 19 (21 in pdf)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T20:07:38-08:00","id":1027997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1027895#post1027895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The products of Blood Sorcery can't be used to sustain life or even unlife&quot;<br /> 1st paragraph under &quot;Creation&quot; in Blood Sorcery pg 19 (21 in pdf)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While that is true under those rules I do like the idea of a vampire being able to use their familiar in such a manner; of course I never particularly liked the rules in the Blood Sorcery book myself, but I figure that's just because of the experience costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:02:59-08:00","id":1028572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1027895#post1027895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;The products of Blood Sorcery can't be used to sustain life or even unlife&amp;quot;<br /> 1st paragraph under &amp;quot;Creation&amp;quot; in Blood Sorcery pg 19 (21 in pdf)</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't have that product, plus it's 1e, not 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:02:59-08:00","id":1028610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1028572#post1028572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't have that product, plus it's 1e, not 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might as well be 2e. 2e's system for Cruac and Theban is a direct port of it, just with the rules for Themes and improvising rituals left out, and the interval for the extended action increased to fix a problem that only exists if you use Themes and improvised rituals. Secrets of the Covenants even included suggested Themes for its new rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:27:38-08:00","id":1028618,"title":"","content":"It's been confirmed that, asides from where the core re-establishes rules, Blood Sorcery, Sacraments and Blasphemies is a book ready to use in the 2E world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T13:16:18-08:00","id":1028665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1028618#post1028618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been confirmed that, asides from where the core re-establishes rules, Blood Sorcery, Sacraments and Blasphemies is a book ready to use in the 2E world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have any of the devs commented on the 2E experience costs for dots of themes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T13:17:58-08:00","id":1028666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1028618#post1028618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been confirmed that, asides from where the core re-establishes rules, Blood Sorcery, Sacraments and Blasphemies is a book ready to use in the 2E world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's definitely balanced within game. I've just always been bothered by the fact that using that book makes it feel like I'm forcing players to only focus on Cruac or Theban Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T14:28:37-08:00","id":1028694,"title":"","content":"Should I add it to my to get list then if it's still compatible with 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T14:53:20-08:00","id":1028701,"title":"","content":"Oh, it's definitely a good book to have, and I do use ideas from it. I just don't like all of the specifics of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:10:15-08:00","id":1028731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1028694#post1028694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should I add it to my to get list then if it's still compatible with 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:11:18-08:00","id":1028732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1028666#post1028666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's definitely balanced within game. I've just always been bothered by the fact that using that book makes it feel like I'm forcing players to only focus on Cruac or Theban Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a weird problem to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:24:46-08:00","id":1028864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1028665#post1028665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have any of the devs commented on the 2E experience costs for dots of themes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> None have, but going by the typical translation of costs into 2e, they should be 1xp each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:28:27-08:00","id":1028866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1028732#post1028732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a weird problem to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's admittedly a weird problem; but each theme costs at least three xp, and on top of having to buy rites and each dot of Blood Sorcery the player's probably gonna spend a ton of xp on it. It's mostly a guilty feeling seeing so much xp spent on one thing; it's powerful certainly, but it just feels weird. (XP is based off of conversion charts to 2e, and mostly I'm bothered because of the slow progression characters will have). In my experience by the time a character can really do something with it the game has come to a close. Of course that's mostly just a personal pet peeve, and I still use the system because I absolutely love the improvised and creation ritual systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:48:26-08:00","id":1028872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1028864#post1028864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None have, but going by the typical translation of costs into 2e, they should be 1xp each.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they'd cost 3 experiences each. In 1e they cost 5x new dot, so to translate to 2e experiences we first have to flatten the progression by finding the mean cost per dot, which is 15. Then we divide that by 5 to convert from experience points to experiences, leaving us with 3 per dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T22:12:33-08:00","id":1028876,"title":"","content":"I love Blood Sorceries for 2E purposes, but I use it for designing balanced spells, not having players buy themes and wield free-form magic. I like that vampiric blood sorcery is more static than many other forms of sorcery in-setting, which each Cruac spell needing to be individually created through suffering (ala the 1E CoC book) and all Theban Spells need to be individually discovered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T03:27:42-08:00","id":1028943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1028872#post1028872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they'd cost 3 experiences each. In 1e they cost 5x new dot, so to translate to 2e experiences we first have to flatten the progression by finding the mean cost per dot, which is 15. Then we divide that by 5 to convert from experience points to experiences, leaving us with 3 per dot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh, misread the x5 as x2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:34:10-08:00","id":1029049,"title":"","content":"I've personally found that the Themes combined with 2e's casting system (read: slow) actually works out pretty nicely, balance-wise. The ritual disciplines give you a wide array of effects in exchange for being a preparation-based power type, so you still need normal disciplines for many things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:08:28-08:00","id":1029133,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the half hour to cast system makes ritual disciplines a lot less potent than when you were able to get off a ritual in 3 seconds anytime you wanted, plus it makes the mage-like themes version of blood sorceries a lot less plot-ruining and less likely to step on toes. I mean, before my group discovered that 2e overrides the casting time aspect of Blood Sorcery we ran with the 1-turn casting time default and it pretty much meant that anyone not using Cruac, Theban or another kind of Blood Sorcery was going to be overshadowed in some way, even if it was unintentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T19:00:05-08:00","id":1029413,"title":"","content":"Rereading the Void Creatures, they're not actually creations of blood sorcery at all, you open a tiny gateway to their world (probably a lower depths world), thru which they enter ours. The Void Creatures exist before the Cruac Magic summons them. And they are the result of a, Cruac Style merit, not the direct result of a ritual to specifically summon them. So the no feeding from blood sorcery creations rule applies to Cruac Gods and Zombies, and maybe the demonic Theban familiar but not Void Creatures, as you don't create them, you merely release them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T19:11:02-08:00","id":1029420,"title":"","content":"The Vitae is not created by the Cr\u00faac God. It's either offered in the ritual or taken from living beings as it feeds. It is, basically, a Vitae container. Something that is explicitly possible to create with Blood Magic since Vitae Reliquary is a Miracle in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T13:23:48-08:00","id":1029726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1029413#post1029413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rereading the Void Creatures, they're not actually creations of blood sorcery at all, you open a tiny gateway to their world (probably a lower depths world), thru which they enter ours. The Void Creatures exist before the Cruac Magic summons them. And they are the result of a, Cruac Style merit, not the direct result of a ritual to specifically summon them. So the no feeding from blood sorcery creations rule applies to Cruac Gods and Zombies, and maybe the demonic Theban familiar but not Void Creatures, as you don't create them, you merely release them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're going with that but the merit also says that the creature must have blood, which is not a given in a creature that &quot;appears as a strange conglomeration of darkness and animal parts.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:11:33-08:00","id":1033110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1029726#post1029726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see where you're going with that but the merit also says that the creature must have blood, which is not a given in a creature that &amp;quot;appears as a strange conglomeration of darkness and animal parts.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> You can choose to force the Void Creature into a humanoid or animal form when you summon it, so that solves the blood issue, no reason it won't have blood then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:26:33-08:00","id":1033114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1033110#post1033110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can choose to force the Void Creature into a humanoid or animal form when you summon it, so that solves the blood issue, no reason it won't have blood then.</div> </div> </div> </div>A humanoid or animal <i>shape</i>. It's still made of shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:24:42-08:00","id":1033682,"title":"","content":"Given that you can feed on ghosts and other things that don't really have blood I wouldn't say that was an insurmountable problem if the ST OKed it.<br /> As the previews haven't been updated could someone tell me what the third dot of \u017diva does please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:56:11-08:00","id":1033700,"title":"","content":"Enliven the Animal \u2022\u2022\u2022, any time your character would gain a condition from detachment, you can spend will power instead and gain Rapture instead of the condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:19:31-08:00","id":1033749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1033682#post1033682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that you can feed on ghosts and other things that don't really have blood I wouldn't say that was an insurmountable problem if the ST OKed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh... How can you do this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:57:26-08:00","id":1033768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1033700#post1033700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enliven the Animal \u2022\u2022\u2022, any time your character would gain a condition from detachment, you can spend will power instead and gain Rapture instead of the condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1033749#post1033749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhh... How can you do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the vampires problem, the merit (Unnatural Affinity, page 114) acknowledges there may be additional complications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:58:18-08:00","id":1033769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1033749#post1033749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhh... How can you do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Merit that lets you eat other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T18:10:08-08:00","id":1033776,"title":"","content":"The merit only lets you gain vitae from them, it doesn't say how you go about that. The Secrets of the Covenants book has a short note about how in order to drink from a ghost, the Ordo captured it in a containment device that made it solid. You'd still have to go through that process or something else that allows you to actually touch them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12860-your3rdshadow","name":"Your3rdShadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:27:05-08:00","id":1033830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1033769#post1033769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merit that lets you eat other things.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Drawback:</b> This advantage does not inherently mean the character is (more) able to feed from the chosen subject. For example, ghosts exist in an ethereal state, and don\u2019t have physical blood.<br /> <br /> - Pg. 114","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T20:18:45-08:00","id":1033855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1033830#post1033830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This advantage does not inherently mean the character is (more) able to feed from the chosen subject. For example, ghosts exist in an ethereal state, and don\u2019t have physical blood.<br /> <br /> - Pg. 114</div> </div> </div> </div>THAT<br /> <br /> is perfectly fair, I forgot about it, I'm drowning in things, blargurgleburble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T21:12:18-08:00","id":1033871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1033855#post1033855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THAT<br /> <br /> is perfectly fair, I forgot about it, I'm drowning in things, blargurgleburble.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T23:46:00-08:00","id":1033901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1033768#post1033768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is the vampires problem, the merit (Unnatural Affinity, page 114) acknowledges there may be additional complications.</div> </div> </div> </div> Stupid auto correct that was supposed to be Enliven the Anima, not Enliven the Animal. <br /> <br /> And your welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T23:47:25-08:00","id":1033903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1033114#post1033114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A humanoid or animal <i>shape</i>. It's still made of shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div> Shadows in the form of blood you can drink. Void Creatures are only partly shadows to begin with, they also have a mixture of animal parts, whose to say that doesn't include a blood filled heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-18-2017, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:42:41-08:00","id":1034141,"title":"","content":"Why would it be made of blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:35:52-08:00","id":1034173,"title":"","content":"You can give void creatures blood if you want, but we didn't really intend them to have fancy functional circulatory systems. Their most obvious relatives don't have it, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:22:37-08:00","id":1034376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1034141#post1034141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would it be made of blood?</div> </div> </div> </div> Because you plan on eating it, so when you force it to take on physical form, you make sure that includes having blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:29:02-08:00","id":1034378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1034173#post1034173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can give void creatures blood if you want, but we didn't really intend them to have fancy functional circulatory systems. Their most obvious relatives don't have it, so...</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess you intended the Void Creatures to be minions and did not expect someone to look at the rules for them and say hey with the Unnatural Affinity Merit a Character could eat them for Vitae instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T19:18:00-08:00","id":1034406,"title":"","content":"You can force it into a human or animal <i>shape</i>, you don't turn it into an exact copy of a human or an animal. 'It appears as a strange conglomeration of darkness and animal parts.'<br /> <br /> Sure you can eat it with Unnatural Affinity, but it's not the wisest choice to spend that Merit on. Void creatures have Health equal to 2 + dots of the Ritual used. The ritual costs its dots in Vitae. So you can immediately get your Vitae back, and have a severely weakened void creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T22:10:10-08:00","id":1034462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1034376#post1034376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because you plan on eating it, so when you force it to take on physical form, you make sure that includes having blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the wording of the Merit is <i>shape</i>, not <i>form</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:57:02-08:00","id":1035350,"title":"","content":"So are you suggesting they're incorporeal, just look like humanoids or animals, without a physical dimension, because it seems like it was intended that despite being creatures of shadow, at least partly, that when you force them into humaniod or animal shapes that they take on a physical embodyment. I could be wrong, I'll look at it. <br /> <br /> If not, I can see no reason why the shape you force them into can not include blood if you could. <br /> <br /> It does also beg the question how do Void Creatures feed to obtain vitae, do that drink blood like a, vampire or ghoul, do they drain breath like a strix, or do they devour flesh like a Cruac God? <br /> <br /> I'm inclined to believe as written they function similar to Ghouls in the way they feed, except without the feeding restrictions of only gaining vitae from Vampire blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T17:51:26-08:00","id":1035556,"title":"","content":"The vibe I get is that they're meant to be about as corporeal as the Strix... all shadows and thick smoke that happen to take a vaguely animal-like silhouette of the summoner's choosing. Maybe not intangible, <i>precisely</i>, but no real room for blood or an easy approximation thereof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:20:29-08:00","id":1035832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1035556#post1035556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vibe I get is that they're meant to be about as corporeal as the Strix... all shadows and thick smoke that happen to take a vaguely animal-like silhouette of the summoner's choosing. Maybe not intangible, <i>precisely</i>, but no real room for blood or an easy approximation thereof.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the impression I got as well. And I assumed they only gained Vitae when given it by the vampire that summoned them, or perhaps another willing donor, since no mechanism is given for them to feed independently.Tthough now that someone brings it up I suppose it might make sense for them to use Breath Drinking like the Strix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-21-2017, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T10:54:42-08:00","id":1036713,"title":"","content":"See I assumed that the purpose of forcing to take a animal or humanoid shape was to make them more physically capable, not just as a disguise. <br /> <br /> I mean they aren't pure shadow like the Strix, only partly, with the rest being animal parts which suggests at least some physical parts. <br /> <br /> I think we need some answers on how Void Creatures are supposed to function, as if we don't know how they feed or use vitae and how much vitae can they contain and we don't know if they have a physical embodiment then how can we properly use them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:38:36-08:00","id":1036848,"title":"","content":"There are several powers in SotC that could do with some clarification and I agree this is one of them, although we do have Rose's response.<br /> <br /> My thoughts were always that Vitae is distilled/concentrated life essence. It just doesn't seem sensible to me that a void creature would produce such a thing &quot;naturally.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:16:11-08:00","id":1036994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1036848#post1036848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are several powers in SotC that could do with some clarification and I agree this is one of them, although we do have Rose's response.<br /> <br /> My thoughts were always that Vitae is distilled/concentrated life essence. It just doesn't seem sensible to me that a void creature would produce such a thing &amp;quot;naturally.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> But Ghosts do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:21:01-08:00","id":1036997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1034173#post1034173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can give void creatures blood if you want, but we didn't really intend them to have fancy functional circulatory systems. Their most obvious relatives don't have it, so...</div> </div> </div> </div> If this is Roses comment that you are referring to, it doesn't really tell me how they gain and store vitae, it does in dictate that if you can give them blood, but I don't know if she means when shaping them, or giving them some else's blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:12:59-08:00","id":1038003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1036994#post1036994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Ghosts do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familliar with the Geist books so I couldn't comment on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1036997#post1036997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If this is Roses comment that you are referring to, it doesn't really tell me how they gain and store vitae, it does in dictate that if you can give them blood, but I don't know if she means when shaping them, or giving them some else's blood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, she's saying that they didn't intend for them to do this but if the ST wants to, then have at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:17:32-08:00","id":1038007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1036994#post1036994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Ghosts do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts don't produce Vitae, the ability of vampires to make Vitae from their Corpus does not mean their Corpus has Vitae in it. Vitae is something vampires manufacture out of the life energy of of other beings. This energy is primarily taken through blood, but with enough adaptation can be taken in through other means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-25-2017, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T14:38:23-08:00","id":1038046,"title":"","content":"Of course, there's no ability in official 2e material that actually makes it possible for vampires to gain Vitae from a ghost. If you home brew one though, Unnatural Affinity will allow you to count it as vampire Vitae for the purposes of feeding restrictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T14:45:32-08:00","id":1038047,"title":"","content":"Well, Materialized ghosts as well as ghosts in the Underworld (or any other place where there is no Twilight) should be fair game. And any vampire with Dominate or Majesty could &quot;convince&quot; the ghost to Materialize or open an Avernian Gate (if that ghost has those Manifestations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:25:19-08:00","id":1038068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1038047#post1038047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Materialized ghosts as well as ghosts in the Underworld (or any other place where there is no Twilight) should be fair game. And any vampire with Dominate or Majesty could &amp;quot;convince&amp;quot; the ghost to Materialize or open an Avernian Gate (if that ghost has those Manifestations).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point, I hadn't considered Materialize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:40:58-08:00","id":1038079,"title":"","content":"But there is a lack of options for vampires if they stumble upon ghosts that doesn't have the Materialize Manifestation. The only power for vampires to actually interact with ghosts in Twilight is Pseshkf from 2E's Obtenebration, and it doesn't exactly allow for feeding (and is Bloodline exclusive). But it shouldn't be too hard to come up with some ritual for Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery that allows the vampire to physically interact with ghosts as if they were corporeal until the next sunrise, or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:04:40-08:00","id":1038139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1038079#post1038079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is a lack of options for vampires if they stumble upon ghosts that doesn't have the Materialize Manifestation. The only power for vampires to actually interact with ghosts in Twilight is Pseshkf from 2E's Obtenebration, and it doesn't exactly allow for feeding (and is Bloodline exclusive). But it shouldn't be too hard to come up with some ritual for Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery that allows the vampire to physically interact with ghosts as if they were corporeal until the next sunrise, or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or following the Ordo story example, use some kind of Occult or Science check to make a device capable of containing one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12860-your3rdshadow","name":"Your3rdShadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:14:41-08:00","id":1038143,"title":"","content":"That's really not a bad idea. And my character is already interested in ghosts to have gotten Unnatural Affinity for them as well as a homebrewed non-exclusive update of Essentiaphagia. What do you think is the basis of that machine? Is it a tool of a Scale? If so, to which Mystery would such a Scale belong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:36:41-08:00","id":1038157,"title":"","content":"Probably a Scale. Likely Zirnitra, but I could maybe see Voivode. Or it might be one of those scales of a Coil that doesn't even exist yet, as implied by the book to be a thing. Probably also a few homebrew Mysteries it'd fit with.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it might be some warped, ordo-ized Summoning ritual that materializes a ghost in the form of immobile goop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:29:53-08:00","id":1038247,"title":"","content":"That Ordo story even gives you the recipe to do so. It includes jelly fish. I think once you take unnatural affinity, it's just a matter of role playing how you get access to it. <br /> <br /> I think maybe instead of referring to it as life force, one should call it animating force, which Vampires can convert to Vitae to animate themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T23:22:08-08:00","id":1039846,"title":"","content":"Making my way through and am at the back of the book...but I'm kind of confused with the Theban Sorcery Miracles. <br /> <br /> In each Miracle, next to the dot value there's an additional prerequisite next to it. Stuff like &quot;Divination 1&quot;, &quot;Destruction 2&quot;, &quot;Protection 3&quot;, etc. Trouble is, the book doesn't explain what this extra prerequisite is. Turning to my copy of VtR2 yields nothing, since that prerequisite isn't even listed in that book's Miracles. Not even its' index. <br /> <br /> So...what is it? <br /> <br /> If it's something from 1e...yeah I came on during 2e and have no idea what it could be if it was something from an older book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T23:59:27-08:00","id":1039854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1039846#post1039846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making my way through and am at the back of the book...but I'm kind of confused with the Theban Sorcery Miracles.<br /> <br /> In each Miracle, next to the dot value there's an additional prerequisite next to it. Stuff like &quot;Divination 1&quot;, &quot;Destruction 2&quot;, &quot;Protection 3&quot;, etc. Trouble is, the book doesn't explain what this extra prerequisite is. Turning to my copy of VtR2 yields nothing, since that prerequisite isn't even listed in that book's Miracles. Not even its' index.<br /> <br /> So...what is it?<br /> <br /> If it's something from 1e...yeah I came on during 2e and have no idea what it could be if it was something from an older book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is a reference to Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies, a 1e book written with 2e in mind. The short story is the book contains rules for blood sorcery, and other stuff too, that allow for creating your own rituals using themes like Divination, Destruction, Protection, etc. What you see in Secrets of the Covenants is not prerequisites as much as how they created the ritual using the rules from Blood Sorcery. You could use the book with 2e rules on actually casting spells if rituals are of great interest. Otherwise, you can just ignore the references.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T00:11:36-08:00","id":1039859,"title":"","content":"Of note, the listed themes aren't even close enough to do the listed effects for most of those rituals (especially on thebans end). So it feels kinda like a last minute addon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T00:30:19-08:00","id":1039866,"title":"","content":"The writer probably created the rituals then decided dots and themes, but I assume the limitations from the book were kept in mind. I don't know if I implied otherwise at this late hour. I scratched my head for some of the rituals during the preview, but I don't do game design, so I leave it to others to second guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T07:39:17-08:00","id":1039982,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if we take the theme dot levels and target numbers of successes for the SotC rites and miracles as accurate, it's clear that these Themes must be far more potent in 2e. I'd love to see a Blood Sorcery 2e that brings the creative casting rules more in line with the newly broadened capabilities of the ritual Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T08:04:04-08:00","id":1039992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1039982#post1039982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if we take the theme dot levels and target numbers of successes for the SotC rites and miracles as accurate, it's clear that these Themes must be far more potent in 2e. I'd love to see a Blood Sorcery 2e that brings the creative casting rules more in line with the newly broadened capabilities of the ritual Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would absolutely love that, myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:55:54-08:00","id":1040059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1039854#post1039854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a reference to Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies, a 1e book written with 2e in mind. The short story is the book contains rules for blood sorcery, and other stuff too, that allow for creating your own rituals using themes like Divination, Destruction, Protection, etc. What you see in Secrets of the Covenants is not prerequisites as much as how they created the ritual using the rules from Blood Sorcery. You could use the book with 2e rules on actually casting spells if rituals are of great interest. Otherwise, you can just ignore the references.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Looking at its DRPG entry online while its' PDF is dirt cheap...yeah, I'm in no real rush to get it. Don't exactly have a VtR2 game planned in the near future, but I'll file it away for future reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 01-29-2017, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T11:25:29-08:00","id":1040108,"title":"","content":"A 2E Bloody Sorcery book that reworks the system completely is #1 on my wishlist for Vampire. Maybe across all of 2E, and Vampire isn't even in my top 3 favorite games (but is still well liked).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:52:31-08:00","id":1040357,"title":"","content":"It seems that blood sorcery that is not Theban defaults to some form of Cruac. I would like to see Kindred Vodoun updated along with other blood sorcery from around the world. Maybe a book that includes such things could find space to expand on Themes and revisit creative casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:12:47-08:00","id":1041268,"title":"","content":"I love that the Invictus are mightiest when they get <i>married</i>. Sure, it just takes two consenting adults and a Notary, but you <i>just</i> know that the Invictus use it as an excuse to party and show off.<br /> <br /> <b>Plot seed:</b> Your Sire is getting married. Yes, you're expected to be there. Yes, you have to bring a present. Oh, yeah, and he's marrying someone related to someone you really, <i>really</i> hate.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> OK, more seriously - the Invictus Superman is <i>really</i> doable:<br /> <br /> 1. Swear an Oath of the True Knight.<br /> 2. Swear an Oath of Office.<br /> 3. Take Noblesse Oblige.<br /> 4. ???<br /> 5. Profit!<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Oh, and you can pick up Stigmata with the Coil of Zirnitra. Just sayin'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:06:52-08:00","id":1041547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1041268#post1041268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love that the Invictus are mightiest when they get <i>married</i>. Sure, it just takes two consenting adults and a Notary, but you <i>just</i> know that the Invictus use it as an excuse to party and show off.<br /> <br /> <b>Plot seed:</b> Your Sire is getting married. Yes, you're expected to be there. Yes, you have to bring a present. Oh, yeah, and he's marrying someone related to someone you really, <i>really</i> hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically appropriate, considering the Invictus' MO. And loving that plot hook there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:27:48-08:00","id":1041816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1038079#post1038079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is a lack of options for vampires if they stumble upon ghosts that doesn't have the Materialize Manifestation. The only power for vampires to actually interact with ghosts in Twilight is Pseshkf from 2E's Obtenebration, and it doesn't exactly allow for feeding (and is Bloodline exclusive). But it shouldn't be too hard to come up with some ritual for Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery that allows the vampire to physically interact with ghosts as if they were corporeal until the next sunrise, or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which book is Pseshkf in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:46:56-08:00","id":1041914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013865-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1041816#post1041816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which book is Pseshkf in?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">The blog</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T11:06:34-08:00","id":1041928,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#5A5A5A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Grazie, I really like it one of my favorite clans in V:tM was the Lasombra and I am so glad to see this.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T23:46:44-08:00","id":1042252,"title":"","content":"So this might have been discussed earlier in this thread but is it me or is the blood god kind of meh. For all the effort and resources you put in you just get a strong vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:32:01-08:00","id":1043188,"title":"","content":"The Blood God has a few advantages over Kindred. One it can be crazy massive if enough vitae is invested in it during it creation. It can feed on any flesh, so it lacks the feeding restrictions of Kindred, you can feed it kibble and bits which it inflicts lethal damage on feeding. <br /> <br /> It's a designer being so you have control over it's form that you don't get with just embracing someone. <br /> <br /> And it doesn't have a humanity stat, so it never has to fear getting 0 humanity. <br /> <br /> And best of all, the same vampires that made it can bring it back to unlife if it's killed or banished from the earth by conducting the rite again this time more powerful then it used to be if they choose.<br /> <br /> It has a humaniod form, but that doesn't mean human, it could have antlers, a mouth of sharp fangs, three eyes, multiple genitals, flowers, four arms, as long as it remains humaniod. A head, arms, torso, legs.<br /> <br /> Its powerful, costumizable, and far, far less human then any Kindred, it has far more flexuble deit then Kindred and if its creators exist they can use the same rite to make it to resurrect it. Its basically the Vampire equivilant of a Prommie.<br /> <br /> Blood Gods also can't embrace, create ghouls, but if they are created with Cruac 5 the can create other Blood Gods and other weird stuff. <br /> <br /> Even weird if one of their creators has the Primal Creation Cruac Style they can get pregnate, possibly giving born to a very weird Dampyr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-03-2017, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:46:51-08:00","id":1045487,"title":"","content":"One curious question?<br /> <br /> What rituals do you think a Chorister is likely to be taught or to seek out... Id go with &quot;The Pool of Forbidden Truths&quot; <br /> <br /> as A. it could give a member of the Invictus or Carthians help with their manifold problems... and could help to enlighten their souls, thus hopefully slowly but surely pushing them towards the circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T16:12:17-08:00","id":1047971,"title":"","content":"It all depends on why they joined the CoC for what goals, and what rituals are available. <br /> <br /> If they have any powers that benefit from higher presence, they may want to go with one that boosts presence, if they want more secrets, they may go with pools of forbidden truths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}